    "answer": {
      "short": "Translate $y=\\sin x$ right by $\\frac\\pi4,\\frac\\pi2,\\frac{3\\pi}4,\\pi$. Every curve has amplitude $1$ and period $2\\pi$.",
      "worked": "For $y=\\sin(x-h)$, translate each sine key point right by $h$. Zeros occur at $x=h+k\\pi$, maxima at $x=h+\\frac\\pi2+2k\\pi$, and minima at $x=h+\\frac{3\\pi}2+2k\\pi$. Use $h=0,\\frac\\pi4,\\frac\\pi2,\\frac{3\\pi}4,\\pi$, keeping only points in $[0,2\\pi]$ and including both domain endpoints. Join smoothly on common axes.",
      "solutionDiagrams": [
